===Verb===
{{en-verb|*|head=[[ruffle]] [[some]] [[feather]]s}}

# {{lb|en|informal|figuratively}} To cause a [[disturbance]]; to [[arouse]] resentment, [[anger]], or [[concern]].
#: {{ux|en|Any frank discussion of politics is sure to '''ruffle some feathers'''.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=28 Aug 76|volume=4|number=9|journal=Gay Community News|page=11|author=David P. Brill|title=Talking Politics|text=Plainclothes vice squad detectives played the [gay] bars and waited to be propositioned, or asked out, or something, and bang! According to those old enough to remember {{...}} the police found themselves arresting legislators, employees of the mayor's office, and even some off-duty cops. So many prominent '''feathers were ruffled''' that it was decided that Beantown's police had better tend to more important, but less personally risky, endeavors.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|work=FT Weekend|date=2023-09-30|title=The wildest job in Silicon Valley|author=Hannah Murphy|section=Life & Arts|page=17|passage=Asking multiple territorial sales teams to share ideas and resources '''ruffled feathers'''.}}

